  "output": "Ran `deadlock_sim.py` against `migration.db`. A lock-cycle error occurred and output was captured to `deadlock_output.txt`.\n\n**Deadlock error message:**\n```\n[A] FAILED: database is locked\n```\n(sqlite3.OperationalError: `database is locked`, i.e. SQLITE_BUSY on connection A when it tried to upgrade its lock to update account 2)\n\nFull captured output:\n```\nDB: migration.db | A: 1 -> 2 | B: 2 -> 1\n\n[A] FAILED: database is locked\n[B] locked account 2, sleeping 0.10s ...\n[B] committed\n\nFinal balances: account 1 = 110, account 2 = 90\nOutcome: {'A': 'failed: database is locked', 'B': 'committed'}\n```\n\nNote: Thread B won the race and committed its transfer, so `migration.db` balances are now account 1 = 110, account 2 = 90. Thread A rolled back cleanly, so no partial state remains.",
